            <ArticleTitle>[Bronchopulmonary diseases features in miners of Kolsky Transpolar area].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>35-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Miners engaged into open-cast and underground extraction of copper-nickel ores in Kolsky Transpolar area have chronic bronchitis as a main nosologic entity among chronic bronchopulmonary diseases (19.1% of the workers). Considerably lower (4.0% of the workers) occurrence concerns chronic obstructive lung disease and bronchial asthma, both developed before the occupational involvement (1.3% of the workers). Complex of occupational and nonoccupational risk factors is connected mostly with smoking that increases COLD/CB risk 10.7-15.8-fold.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
